If I'm supposed to give a speech nine months
from now, I already have a folder made on

00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:57.260
my phone, and I just keep adding stuff that
I'm going to talk about in that meeting that's

00:11:57.260 --> 00:11:58.890
nine months from now.

00:11:58.890 --> 00:12:02.490
Nine months of preparation of adding notes
in the phone to prepare for something like

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:03.490
that.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:04.490
That's part of work ethic.

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:05.490
That is work ethic.

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:06.490
#4: Do More.

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:09.200
Let me explain what I mean by do more.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:10.300
I remember I was in an office.

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:11.949
I was brand-spanking new.

00:12:11.949 --> 00:12:17.279
It's 2002, 2003, and I'm in an office of Victory
in Balboa in the city of Encino, California,

00:12:17.279 --> 00:12:24.760
and Saturdays, we were all young, and there
were a bunch of pretty girls in the office

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:27.449
and everybody's Saturday night wanted to go
to Dublins.

00:12:27.449 --> 00:12:29.430
Dublins was the place to be.

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:31.190
Everybody wanted to go to Dublins.

00:12:31.190 --> 00:12:33.329
You wanted to go to Saddle Ranch and Miyagi's.

00:12:33.329 --> 00:12:34.870
It was all in the same corner.

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:36.870
Like literally 300 yards away.

00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:39.500
You go to Dublins, across the street, Miyagi's
and you go to Saddle Ranch.

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:40.500
Boom, boom, boom boom.

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:43.720
If you wanted to go to after hours, you could.

00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:45.620
Everybody wanted to go clubbing on Saturday
night.

00:12:45.620 --> 00:12:49.690
And I was in the office, 5:00 everyone's leaving.

00:12:49.690 --> 00:12:51.100
6:00 two people left.

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:52.949
7:00, I'm staying.

00:12:52.949 --> 00:12:53.949
No one's there.

00:12:53.949 --> 00:12:54.949
8:00, I'm staying.

00:12:54.949 --> 00:12:55.949
9:00, I'm staying.

00:12:55.949 --> 00:12:57.029
10, I'm staying.

00:12:57.029 --> 00:12:58.029
Everyone's gone.

00:12:58.029 --> 00:12:59.029
11 I'm staying.

00:12:59.029 --> 00:13:01.750
By that time, I'm so wiped out I'm not going
to the club.

00:13:01.750 --> 00:13:03.769
I'm going home, reading a book, going to sleep.

00:13:03.769 --> 00:13:04.769
Boring to you, right?

00:13:04.769 --> 00:13:05.769
That's boring to you, right?

00:13:05.769 --> 00:13:09.470
Now fast forward and ask me what places I've
partied and had fun with.

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:11.779
You won't even believe half the stories if
I told you.

00:13:11.779 --> 00:13:14.040
You would think I'm telling you a story out
of a movie.

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:18.970
There's no way in the world you partied with
prime ministers and princes and governors

00:13:18.970 --> 00:13:23.251
and senators and billionaires and all this
other stuff, because I didn't want to get

00:13:23.251 --> 00:13:24.339
too excited about Dublins.

00:13:24.339 --> 00:13:25.720
There was a time when that was exciting to
me.

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:27.620
There was a time Miyagi's was exciting to
me.

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:29.600
There was a time when all that stuff was exciting
to me.

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:35.780
Again, how big is your purpose, how long will
you put your activity with the efforts, and

00:13:35.780 --> 00:13:38.930
then does it match the standard of behavior
that you want to put out.

00:13:38.930 --> 00:13:39.930
So do more.

00:13:39.930 --> 00:13:42.149
If a person leaves at 6:00, you leave at 8:00.

00:13:42.149 --> 00:13:45.240
If a person makes 100 calls a day, you make
200 calls a day.

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:48.500
If a person makes 50 contacts a day, you make
75.

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:53.380
If a person sells 20 of your product, you
sell 40.

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:57.620
If somebody practices three hours, you practice
five hours.

00:13:57.620 --> 00:14:00.620
If somebody practices six hours, you practice
eight hours.

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:03.139
If someone reads two books, you read four
books.

00:14:03.139 --> 00:14:05.630
Just do a little bit more.

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:08.279
Do a little bit more.

00:14:08.279 --> 00:14:12.300
#5: Subscribe to the "Now" mentality.

00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:13.760
We'll call them tomorrow.

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:14.760
No.

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:15.760
We're calling them now.

00:14:15.760 --> 00:14:19.100
So the other day, one of my guys, his name
is Fred, he calls me.

00:14:19.100 --> 00:14:23.820
He said, "Hey man, I'm kind of disappointed,
you know, because the office lease that I

00:14:23.820 --> 00:14:28.030
wanted didn't go through" And this is commercial
real estate agent that he's flopped with me

00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:29.180
three times.

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:31.459
And I've made this guy $200,000.

00:14:31.459 --> 00:14:34.210
Three times he's let down referrals that I
gave this guy.

00:14:34.210 --> 00:14:37.519
I don't do well with people who I give referrals
to.

00:14:37.519 --> 00:14:40.660
I expect perfection from somebody I give a
referral to, right?

00:14:40.660 --> 00:14:41.980
I'm going to make you money.

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:43.161
That's a market I'm introducing you to.

00:14:43.161 --> 00:14:45.120
My credibility is on the line.

00:14:45.120 --> 00:14:46.120
This guy did it three times.

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:47.130
I said, what did he do?

00:14:47.130 --> 00:14:49.029
He said, "Well, you know, we're just not getting
the deal."

00:14:49.029 --> 00:14:50.190
I texted him.

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:52.470
Right there, while I'm on the phone with the
speaker, I texted the commercial real estate

00:14:52.470 --> 00:14:53.470
agent.

00:14:53.470 --> 00:14:54.470
He doesn't respond.

00:14:54.470 --> 00:14:55.470
I call his office.

00:14:55.470 --> 00:14:56.470
He doesn't respond.

00:14:56.470 --> 00:14:57.470
I call his phone.

00:14:57.470 --> 00:14:58.470
He doesn't respond.

00:14:58.470 --> 00:15:00.160
I ask to talk to his supervisor.

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:01.440
I talked to his supervisor.

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:03.250
I said, who's the owner of the company?

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:04.610
They put me on the phone with the owner of
the company.

00:15:04.610 --> 00:15:06.380
I talked to the president of the company.

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:08.420
The president of the company got a call from
me.

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:11.100
Within one hour, I got a call back from everybody.

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:13.180
I got a text back from everybody.

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:19.509
The guy, Fred, ended up getting exactly what
he wanted, from the office, all the expectations,

00:15:19.509 --> 00:15:22.530
they lowered it from a five-year lease to
a three-year lease.

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:23.530
Why?

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:24.530
Because it's do it now.

00:15:24.530 --> 00:15:26.149
Do you know what was the craziest thing Fred
told me?

00:15:26.149 --> 00:15:28.490
Oh my gosh, I'm a little bit nervous.

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:29.490
Why are you nervous?

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:31.670
Because I can't believe you did all that stuff
in 10 minutes.

00:15:31.670 --> 00:15:34.630
I said, "It's called the do-it-now mentality."

00:15:34.630 --> 00:15:36.470
Why would we wait until tomorrow?

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:38.240
Hey, Pat, there's someone that may be interested.

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:39.240
Let's call them right now.

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:40.240
Do you have their phone number?

00:15:40.240 --> 00:15:41.240
Let's call him.

00:15:41.240 --> 00:15:42.240
Yes, let's call him right now.

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:43.240
What are you talking about?

00:15:43.240 --> 00:15:45.380
Let's call him right now.

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:47.069
Do it now mentality.

00:15:47.069 --> 00:15:48.509
Work ethic is a part of it.

00:15:48.509 --> 00:15:49.509
Do it now.

00:15:49.509 --> 00:15:50.509
Not tomorrow.

00:15:50.509 --> 00:15:51.509
Do it now.

00:15:51.509 --> 00:15:52.509
Now.

00:15:52.509 --> 00:15:53.509
Let's do it right now.

00:15:53.509 --> 00:15:55.420
Procrastinate tomorrow, next day, three hours,
five hours, let's do it right now.

00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:57.019
#6: Find Running Mates.

00:15:57.019 --> 00:15:59.850
I love people that work as hard as me and
they push me.

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:01.209
There's nothing like it.

00:16:01.209 --> 00:16:02.209
I love running mates.

00:16:02.209 --> 00:16:04.269
I love people that say, "Pat, five more reps."

00:16:04.269 --> 00:16:05.389
Dude, I'm tired.

00:16:05.389 --> 00:16:06.389
Pat!

00:16:06.389 --> 00:16:07.389
Five more reps!

00:16:07.389 --> 00:16:08.790
Because some days you don't feel like it.

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:10.459
Pat, c'mon, Pat.

00:16:10.459 --> 00:16:11.459
Five more reps.

00:16:11.459 --> 00:16:12.459
C'mon.

00:16:12.459 --> 00:16:13.630
My shoulders are giving out.

00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:15.389
Four more, three more.

00:16:15.389 --> 00:16:16.389
C'mon, Pat.

00:16:16.389 --> 00:16:18.050
C'mon, 10 more calls.

00:16:18.050 --> 00:16:19.519
Running mates.

00:16:19.519 --> 00:16:21.170
Running mates will push each other.

00:16:21.170 --> 00:16:22.459
Running mates will push each other.

00:16:22.459 --> 00:16:25.590
There's nothing like finding a good running
mate that pushes you.

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:28.380
Working hard buddies, if you want to call
it that.

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:32.279
And then eventually, unfortunately, sometimes
you end up not finding anybody else that wants

00:16:32.279 --> 00:16:36.350
to work at your pace, and then you're working
buddies may not be in the same place you're

00:16:36.350 --> 00:16:37.350
at.

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:38.480
They may be a complete different place.

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:39.550
And you play games with each other.

00:16:39.550 --> 00:16:40.550
Hey, what time are you waking up?

00:16:40.550 --> 00:16:41.550
What time are you doing this?

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:43.060
That's your working buddies.

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:46.840
#7: Don't fall for the work smart only concept.

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:50.569
Four hour work week is work smart.

00:16:50.569 --> 00:16:51.569
I get it.

00:16:51.569 --> 00:16:52.569
I respect it.

00:16:52.569 --> 00:16:54.019
Some people like that.

00:16:54.019 --> 00:16:55.019
Standard of behavior.

00:16:55.019 --> 00:16:56.680
Your morals, your standards.

00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:58.139
It's fine.

00:16:58.139 --> 00:17:00.470
Nothing big has ever been built without working
very hard.

00:17:00.470 --> 00:17:01.470
And I'm talking very hard.

00:17:01.470 --> 00:17:02.470
Very hard.

00:17:02.470 --> 00:17:04.530
It's Friday night right now when we're shooting
this.

00:17:04.530 --> 00:17:05.530
Everybody's gone from the office.

00:17:05.530 --> 00:17:09.240
Dennis is here, former 8-year DPT, Dallas
Police Department.

00:17:09.240 --> 00:17:10.240
I'm here.

00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:11.240
We're shooting this.

00:17:11.240 --> 00:17:15.670
I am willing to bet everyone's out of the
office, except for Mario and probably Paul

00:17:15.670 --> 00:17:16.800
is sitting somewhere as well.

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:17.800
It's Friday night.

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:20.390
It's already 7:00.

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:21.410
Everyone's going out to dinner.

00:17:21.410 --> 00:17:24.040
I just got back from Burbank, California.

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:25.209
I was in Bakersfield, California.

00:17:25.209 --> 00:17:27.350
I was in Houston, Texas.

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:29.020
I got a bunch of other travel that's coming
up.

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:30.020
We're here right now in the office.

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:31.020
Why are we doing this?

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:32.020
Well, Pat!

00:17:32.020 --> 00:17:34.050
How do you find the time to shoot these episodes?

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:37.630
You never miss a Tuesday and Thursday episode
of Valuetainment.

00:17:37.630 --> 00:17:41.820
Because some nights on Friday night I want
to go home and kick it and relax and I don't

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:45.700
and we shoot these episodes because we're
supposed to come to you Tuesdays and Thursdays.

00:17:45.700 --> 00:17:50.230
And do you realize from the moment we said
Tuesdays and Thursdays, we've never, ever

00:17:50.230 --> 00:17:53.000
done an episode that we missed on Tuesday
or Thursday.

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:54.000
Why?

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:55.090
It's part of commitment.

00:17:55.090 --> 00:17:56.510
It's part of being predictable.

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:57.670
It's part of showing up.

00:17:57.670 --> 00:18:00.521
And there are days, right now, my back, I'm
not gonna lie to you.

00:18:00.521 --> 00:18:02.750
We did legs with my personal trainer, Josh.

00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:06.620
My hamstrings are so tight right now, Mario
was stretching me right now.

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:08.550
I can't even go like that right now.

00:18:08.550 --> 00:18:11.300
I come up and I can't breathe.

00:18:11.300 --> 00:18:12.300
It's that bad.

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:13.340
Not because of my lower back pain.

00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:14.470
My hamstrings.

00:18:14.470 --> 00:18:15.890
It doesn't matter.

00:18:15.890 --> 00:18:18.860
So when people tell me, but I'm sick, I have
this, I have that.

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:21.250
Then this [work ethic] is not your game yet.

00:18:21.250 --> 00:18:25.320
Then this is not your game yet.

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:28.490
#8: Cut distractions.

00:18:28.490 --> 00:18:29.690
Very simple.

00:18:29.690 --> 00:18:30.730
You've got to cut distractions.

00:18:30.730 --> 00:18:32.870
You're still going to have some distractions
in your life.

00:18:32.870 --> 00:18:36.610
But you've got to cut the distractions that
you can cut.

00:18:36.610 --> 00:18:38.020
Get rid of the distractions.

00:18:38.020 --> 00:18:43.360
Get rid of the, in the office, you know there's
a lot of different stuff that can take time

00:18:43.360 --> 00:18:44.360
away from me.

00:18:44.360 --> 00:18:45.360
I don't want it.

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:46.360
I want to cut distractions.

00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:49.140
I want to cut any kind of distractions I can
cut in my life.

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:51.250
I don't want to deal with office politics.

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:52.640
I want to perform.

00:18:52.640 --> 00:18:54.150
So there's office politics.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:55.150
You go perform.

00:18:55.150 --> 00:18:56.150
You don't need to deal with it.

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:57.440
You go grow your business.

00:18:57.440 --> 00:18:59.630
#9: Absolute focus.

00:18:59.630 --> 00:19:01.100
Absolute focus.

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:08.310
This is tiring, but believe me, I'm the ADHD
guy and you know how ADHDs don't know how

00:19:08.310 --> 00:19:09.310
to focus.

00:19:09.310 --> 00:19:11.400
I'm the guy that would see something, and
I'm gone.

00:19:11.400 --> 00:19:13.660
Boom, I'm looking at all this other stuff.

00:19:13.660 --> 00:19:15.260
You've got to train your mind to be focused.

00:19:15.260 --> 00:19:16.340
It's a muscle.

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:18.080
You've got to train your mind to be focused.

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:19.080
You can do it.

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:23.060
So when people tell me all these rhetoric,
I need to take this medicine, I need to take

00:19:23.060 --> 00:19:24.630
that medicine, stop.

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:25.790
You're looking for an out.

00:19:25.790 --> 00:19:26.930
You may need to take that medicine.

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:28.570
I'm not questioning your doctor.

00:19:28.570 --> 00:19:33.310
All I'm telling you is, stop making excuses
that you can't stay focused.

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:34.310
Practice it.

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:35.310
It's a muscle.

00:19:35.310 --> 00:19:36.310
Stay focused.

00:19:36.310 --> 00:19:37.310
Next, have a to-do list.

00:19:37.310 --> 00:19:38.310
Work ethic has to do with to-do lists.

00:19:38.310 --> 00:19:39.310
What needs to get done next.

00:19:39.310 --> 00:19:40.720
What needs to get done next right now?

00:19:40.720 --> 00:19:44.180
Mario and I, about four hours ago I told him,
I said, "Mario," Mario wanted to add another

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:45.950
project to our list of projects.

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:47.540
I said, let me show you what we got.

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:48.540
That's all I did to him.

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:49.540
I said, let me show it to you.

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:51.460
I went through every single thing and he said,
"Pat, I've got the point."

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:53.170
I said, You want to add another thing?

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:54.170
Here's what we got.

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:55.170
What else do you want to do?

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:56.170
What else do you want to do?

00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:57.170
Can you handle this?

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:58.370
No, we're not ready yet.

00:19:58.370 --> 00:19:59.760
Let's wait 90 more days.

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:01.540
Let's wait 90 more days.

00:20:01.540 --> 00:20:02.610
Next, eat right.

00:20:02.610 --> 00:20:06.080
Work ethic requires energy for you to be able
to last a long time.

00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:11.840
Stamina, efficiency, for you to be able to
go and you have the, you know, you're not

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:13.440
getting tired by 4:00.

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:16.760
If you eat right, you're going to be able
to stick around even longer.

00:20:16.760 --> 00:20:17.780
#12: Plug the leaks.

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:19.400
I don't like leaks.

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:25.740
When I worked at Bally's, I told a story about
Bally's earlier, but when I worked at Bally's,

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:29.070
I wanted to find out where the leaks were.

00:20:29.070 --> 00:20:30.750
It doesn't matter what the leaks were.

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:34.200
The leaks were some of the tours were taking
way too long.

00:20:34.200 --> 00:20:37.460
So the person coming back, he was giving a
forty minute tour of the gym.

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:38.920
You could do that in 13 minutes.

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:40.210
Why are you doing a forty-minute tour?

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:41.440
Just because she's pretty?

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:43.641
We just lost 37 minutes, 27 minutes of your
time.

00:20:43.641 --> 00:20:45.640
I need you to be back here making calls.

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:46.890
This is why we're not hitting our goal.

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:47.920
So plug the leaks.

00:20:47.920 --> 00:20:48.920
What's the leak?

00:20:48.920 --> 00:20:53.380
The leak is, you know, when I make the call,
I'm doing this and I'm doing this and I'm

00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:54.380
doing this.

00:20:54.380 --> 00:20:55.510
That took seven seconds.

00:20:55.510 --> 00:20:56.510
Plug the leaks.

00:20:56.510 --> 00:20:57.510
It's a waste of my time.

00:20:57.510 --> 00:20:58.510
What's the leak?

00:20:58.510 --> 00:21:00.100
Another leak is I'm going from here to here.

00:21:00.100 --> 00:21:03.320
I'm going to find the fastest way to get home,
or I'm.

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:04.990
. . plug whatever leaks you got with your
